{"name":"Athens","hex":"#3f74b1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Athens","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The capital city of Greece.","The Greek government."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Greek."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Athens"}],"entries":[{"title":"Athens","blocks":[{"text":"Athens is the capital and largest city of Greece. A significant coastal urban area in the Mediterranean, Athens is also the capital of the Attica region and is the southernmost capital on the European mainland. With its urban area's population numbering over 3.6 million, it is the eighth-largest urban area in the European Union (EU). The Municipality of Athens, which constitutes a small administrative unit of the entire urban area, had a population of 643,452 in 2021, within its official limits, and a land area of 38.96 square kilometres. Athens joined the UNESCO Global Network of Learning Cities in 2016."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Athens_Acropolis_at_Daybreak.jpg/330px-Athens_Acropolis_at_Daybreak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Athens"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Zappeion_Megaron_on_February_3%2C_2021.jpg/500px-Zappeion_Megaron_on_February_3%2C_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Zappeion_Megaron_on_February_3%2C_2021.jpg/1280px-Zappeion_Megaron_on_February_3%2C_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Zappeion_Megaron_on_February_3%2C_2021.jpg/500px-Zappeion_Megaron_on_February_3%2C_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZappeio